4. REQUIREMENTS 
4.1.  Functional requirements 
4.1.1. Requirements for the set of program’s functions 
The program must: 
1) Perform data reading from Hadoop distributed data storage; 
2) Perform data reading from Oracle distributed data storage; 
3) Perform data saving to Hadoop or Oracle distributed data storage; 
4) Save trained machine learning models; 
5) Load trained machine learning models; 
6) Perform feature computation for machine learning models; 
7) Perform feature selection on the basis of relevance; 
8) Assign fraudulence scores to transactions; 
9) Apply configurations from a file; 
10) Write configurations to a file; 
11) Save model performance metrics; 
12) Save the most relevant features; 
13) Create and save graphs of the EER metric. 
4.1.2. Interface requirements

The software interface must be developed in a form of CLI (command line interface). The interface 
must contain elements giving the operator an option to call the program functionality, namely:  
1) User-help window with a list of available functions; 
2) A set of at least 5 windows for executing parts of the program’s functionality; 
3) A set of commands for altering the program configuration; 
4) A set of commands for starting the program or its parts; 
5) A command for saving the configuration file; 
6) A command for loading the configuration file.

